3.4 Progression and the game loop
- Discoveries. Completion targets are derived from each world’s data: visit every Location; inspect every object of kind inspect or read; hold at least one conversation of three or more exchanges with the primary character; watch each story scene to at least 80 percent.
- Seal of the Era. Progress is completed targets divided by total targets. At 100 percent the player earns the Seal, shown in the journal and on the world card.
- Objective hint line. One line in the HUD naming the nearest undiscovered location, for example “Find the audience hall”. It is calculated from data, never scripted.
- Storage. The browser’s localStorage under the versioned key chronoverse:v1:progress. No accounts and no server storage.
- Nothing is locked. All four worlds are open from the first visit.
3.5 Visual identity
Black, charcoal, warm white and metallic gold. Gold is reserved for interactive or important elements. Panels are frosted glass with a thin gold hairline. No bright colours, no rainbow gradients, no dashboard clutter. Each world adds its own accent from WorldTheme.accent.
