- Motion. 200–400 ms transitions with --cv-ease; fade and slide only; everything switches off under prefers-reduced-motion.
- Contrast. Body text must reach WCAG AA contrast against its panel.
3.6 Language and right-to-left layout
- A language switch sets dir="rtl" or dir="ltr" on the root element.
- Use CSS logical properties everywhere (margin-inline-start, padding-inline, inset-inline-end) instead of left and right.
- Mirror directional icons in RTL (arrows, back buttons) but never mirror the minimap or the 3D view.
- Use Western digits (0–9) in both languages for years and distances.
- Character dialogue is always Modern Standard Arabic. The English line under a subtitle is a translation, never a different answer.
